CCTPBridgeModule_Validate
├── when params length is less than minimum encoding size
│   └── it should return (false, "Invalid params encoding")
├── when params are empty
│   └── it should return (false, "Invalid params encoding")
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return (false, "Zero bridge amount")
├── when token is not USDC
│   └── it should return (false, "Only USDC supported")
├── when mint recipient is zero
│   └── it should return (false, "Zero mint recipient")
├── when finality threshold is invalid
│   └── it should return (false, "Invalid finality threshold")
├── when maxFeeBps equals 10000
│   └── it should return (false, "Invalid max fee bps")
├── when maxFeeBps exceeds 10000
│   └── it should return (false, "Invalid max fee bps")
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return (false, "Insufficient balance")
├── when all checks pass
│   ├── it should return (true, "")
│   └── it should return true for any valid amount [fuzz]
├── validate and execute should agree on failure reasons
│   ├── it should agree on invalid params
│   ├── it should agree on zero bridge amount
│   ├── it should agree on wrong token
│   ├── it should agree on zero mint recipient
│   └── it should agree on invalid max fee bps
└── fuzz: validate and execute agreement
    └── it should produce identical failure reasons for shared validation checks [fuzz]
